{title: Home on the Range}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
Oh, [G]give me a home where the [C]buffalo roam,
Where the [G]deer and the [A7]antelope [D7]play,
Where [G]seldom is [G7]heard a dis[C]couraging word,
And the [G]skies are not [D7]cloudy all [G]day.

{c: Chorus}
[D7]Home, home on the [G]range,
Where the [C]deer and the [A7]antelope [D7]play,
Where [G]seldom is [G7]heard a dis[C]couraging word,
And the [G]skies are not [D7]cloudy all [G]day.
